{"id": "bbb055c1-a268-4ff3-815f-88d8a6e67e24", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll run an assessment of your AgentCore runtimes and gateways across the associated AWS accounts and regions. It will cover VPC/network configuration and encryption settings. I'll summarize the findings when it finishes.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_7HLBkwtJNZ8pFLLFQyex6m", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "agentcore-security-assessment", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["verifying-with-docs", "discovering-topology"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Read-only security assessment of Amazon Bedrock AgentCore runtimes and gateways, focused on (1) VPC/network isolation and (2) encryption. Produce severity-rated findings per resource.",
  "context": "User asked: 'Assess our Bedrock AgentCore runtimes and gateways for VPC and encryption security.' Agent space is in account 012345678901_1, us-east-1 (space ID 542eb1b4-6599-41c3-89f2-9acf843edf01). Use list_associations to find all associated AWS accounts, and check every account. Check all regions where AgentCore is available (start with us-east-1, us-west-2, eu-central-1, ap-southeast-1, ap-southeast-2, eu-west-1, ap-northeast-1, and others the service supports; verify supported regions via docs if unsure). Use the boto3 'bedrock-agentcore-control' client (e.g. list_agent_runtimes, get_agent_runtime, list_agent_runtime_endpoints, list_gateways, get_gateway, list_gateway_targets, get_gateway_target; also memory/code-interpreter/browser if they readily show network mode). READ-ONLY calls only. If an API name or field differs, check the docs with verify_aws_claim.",
  "resources": ["bedrock-agentcore-control: agent runtimes, runtime endpoints, gateways, gateway targets in all associated accounts/regions"],
  "criteria": "VPC/network: for each runtime check networkConfiguration.networkMode (PUBLIC vs VPC); for VPC mode list subnets and security groups and, via ec2 describe_security_groups, flag overly permissive ingress/egress (0.0.0.0/0, all ports); note whether VPC endpoints (interface endpoints for bedrock-agentcore, ECR, S3, CloudWatch Logs) exist in the VPC when relevant. Check inbound authorizer config (authorizerConfiguration: IAM SigV4 vs custom JWT, and whether none/weak) for runtimes and gateways, and protocol/exposure of gateways. Encryption: for gateways check kmsKeyArn (customer-managed KMS key vs AWS-owned default); for runtimes/memory/other resources check any encryption settings exposed; for gateway targets check credentialProviderConfigurations (API key / OAuth / IAM, no plaintext secrets in config), and for target endpoints flag non-HTTPS URLs. For any KMS keys referenced, check rotation status and key state (kms get_key_rotation_status / describe_key). Also check environment variables on runtimes for apparent plaintext secrets (report names only, never values). Also check CloudWatch log group encryption for AgentCore runtime/gateway log groups if found. Output: a table of resources with account/region, a findings list with severity (High/Medium/Low/Info), a summary count, and concise remediation suggestions. Clearly state accounts/regions covered, any that returned access errors, and if no AgentCore resources exist at all say so. Do not print secret values."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Assess AgentCore runtimes and gateways for VPC and encryption security"}], "created_at": null}

